  "answer": "The logic is correct. One edge case to verify: `finishRecord` in `assembler.mjs` sets `state.touched = false` — that field no longer exists but assigning a new property is harmless. `finishField` sets `atFieldStart = true`, which is what we need.\n\nLet me trace the public test `'a,\"say \"' + '\"hi\"\"\"'` = `a,\"say \"\"hi\"\"\"`:\n- `a` → field `a`, inRecord\n- `,` → finishField pushes `a`, atFieldStart true\n- `\"` at field start → quoted\n- `say ` → field `say `\n- `\"` → afterQuote\n- `\"` → literal `\"`, field `say \"`, quoted\n- `hi` → field `say \"hi`\n- `\"` → afterQuote\n- `\"` → literal `\"`, field `say \"hi\"`, quoted\n- `\"` → afterQuote\n- EOF → finishField pushes `say \"hi\"`. Result `[['a','say \"hi\"']]`. ✓\n\nAnd `'a,\"one' + ',two\"\\nb,three'` = `a,\"one,two\"\\nb,three`:\n- quoted field `one,two`, `\"`→afterQuote, `\\n`→endRecord pushes `['a','one,two']`, then `b,three` → `['b','three']`. ✓\n\nAll correct. The changes are complete and consistent.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in the shared parser state machine (`src/state.mjs` and `src/line.mjs`), which caused chunk-boundary-dependent behavior. I rewrote both files:\n\n**`src/line.mjs`**\n- `consumeLine` now sets `pendingCR` on a CR instead of treating CR and LF identically, so CRLF is recognized as one record ending even when split across chunks.\n- Added `consumePendingCR`, which requires the character after a CR to be LF and otherwise throws `BARE_CR` (including at end of input).\n- `endRecord` now pushes the current field before ending the record, so blank lines parse as `['']` and trailing fields are preserved.\n\n**`src/state.mjs`**\n- Fixed doubled-quote handling: in `afterQuote`, a second `\"` now appends one literal `\"` and returns to `quoted` mode instead of throwing `INVALID_QUOTE`.\n- Replaced the `touched` flag with `inRecord`, set whenever any character of a record is seen and cleared when a record ends, so a final record without a line ending is included while a trailing line ending does not add an extra empty record.\n- `finishState` still reports `BARE_CR` for a dangling CR and `UNTERMINATED_QUOTE` for an open quoted field.\n\n`parseRows`, `readItems`, and `countItems` are unchanged and continue to share the same parser, so both consumers see identical records and errors. The slug/checksum helpers were untouched.\n\n**What was checked:** I traced the grammar cases by hand (empty input, blank lines, LF/CRLF split across chunks, bare CR, doubled quotes across chunks, quote-in-unquoted-text, non-delimiter after closing quote, unterminated quote, final record without newline, trailing newline) and the public test inputs. No tests were executed — there is no shell/test runner available in this environment.",
